From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Idan Freiberg <speidy@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 23:44:12 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] 09426: Add TILE-Gx processor language support

GP-0: Add TILE-Gx processor language support

Add a little-endian TILE-Gx processor module with ELF recognition, bundle-aware disassembly, GCC ABI definitions, and p-code semantics.

Generate the instruction decoder from GNU binutils 2.35.1 opcode tables and test parallel bundle register and control-flow behavior.

GP-0: Derive TILE-Gx encodings from the Tilera ISA manual

Replace the binutils-based opcode dump with support/tilegx_encodings.txt,
a table extracted from the TILE-Gx ISA manual (Tilera UG401, release
1.3) by support/extract_ug401_encodings.py, and make the SLEIGH
generator consume that table instead of binutils operand numbers. The
manual-derived encodings match the previous ones for every instruction
and pipeline. Re-deriving them also fixes the store-with-add immediate
bit range, makes Y2 stores read rather than write their value register,
and increments the address register in prefetch_add_*.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
